{"Contextual logger middleware dereferences request fields without nil checks, causing potential panics on malformed or test-generated requests with nil req when accessing req.PluginContext": 0.186078742146492, "Logger middleware ordering issue: NewLoggerMiddleware runs before NewContextualLoggerMiddleware, causing backend request logs to lose pluginId, endpoint, datasource, and user attributes because context is not yet enriched": 0.13235457241535187, "Logger interface breaking change: Adding FromContext method and changing variadic logging methods from ...interface{} to ...any breaks out-of-tree implementations of pkg/plugins/log.Logger": 0.543932318687439, "Logger.FromContext silently drops contextual attributes for custom logger implementations because grafanaInfraLogWrapper.FromContext only handles *log.ConcreteLogger and falls back to d.New() for other types": 0.6318503022193909, "LoggerMiddleware's reliance on m.logger.FromContext(ctx) can lose existing contextual fields when grafanaInfraLogWrapper.FromContext falls back to a fresh/base logger for non-ConcreteLogger types": 0.5656028985977173, "Test logger FromContext returns NewTestLogger() unconditionally instead of preserving existing test logger state, potentially hiding contextual-logging regressions in tests": 0.5616898536682129}